    "B": "Long-acting bronchodilators are not used as a stand-alone reliever medication in asthma.",
    "C": "Inhaled corticosteroids are preventers, but the term “asthma pill” usually refers to a non-steroidal oral preventer.",
    "D": "Long-acting bronchodilators may be used only in combination therapy, not as the “asthma pill” here.",
    "E": "Oral leukotriene receptor antagonists are non-steroidal preventers and are commonly described as an “asthma pill”."
